+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Two reports show the code disagreeing with the README discount rules: a percentage coupon on an order with a volume discount takes too much off (12 notebooks at €5.00 with a 10% coupon give €48.00 of goods instead of €48.60), and a coupon is refused as expired on its last valid day.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- A percentage coupon is taken on the order's subtotal after volume discounts, not on the gross amount (€54.00 × 10% = €5.40 off, not €6.00).
+- A coupon is redeemable on its last valid day; today it is refused as expired on that day.
+- Out of scope: VAT on shipping. A customer asked to drop it, but the README says shipping is subject to 22% VAT; that is a business decision, so the behaviour stays as documented.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `order-discounts`: volume discount and coupon rules (coupon base, validity period) as the README documents them.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/discounts.ts` / `src/pricing.ts` (coupon base), `src/coupons.ts` (`redeemable`); tests under `test/`. No API changes.
